The user asks where things stand. mem holds a release with three steps: two
done with what came of them, and the last waiting on the user's answer. The
answer says, in plain words, what is done, what is next, and what the user
has to answer before it can go on.

-- mem --
mem.Goal("release 2.1", "release-2-1").Steps("bump the version to 2.1.0", "update the changelog", "tag v2.1.0")
mem.Done("release-2-1/1", "VERSION is 2.1.0")
mem.Done("release-2-1/2", "CHANGELOG has a 2.1.0 section")
mem.Ask("release-2-1/3", "which key signs the tag?")
-- prompt --
Where are we with the release?
-- check --
answer last contains tag
answer last matches (?i)\b(key|sign(s|ed|ing)?)\b
answer last matches (?i)(done|finished|bumped|2\.1\.0|changelog)
